{
  "title": "28: al-Qasas القصص",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓمٓ‏(1)\nTAA SIM MEEM.\nTa, Seen, Meem.\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABIL MOBEEN.\nThese are the signs of the Manifest Book.\nنَتْلُوْا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ نَّبَاِ مُوْسٰى وَفِرْعَوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ لِقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(3)\nNATLOO A’LAYKA MIN NABAE MOOSAA WA FIRA’UNA BIL-HAQQE LEQAWMIYN YOAMENOON.\nWe relate to you truly some of the account of Moses and Pharaoh for a people who have faith.\nاِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ عَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَجَعَلَ اَهْلَهَا شِيَعًا يَّسْتَضْعِفُ طَآئِفَةً مِّنْهُمْ يُذَبِّحُ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْىٖ نِسَآءَهُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(4)\nINNA FIR-A’UNA A’LAA FIL ARZE WA JA-A’LA AHLAHAA SHEYA-A’YN YASTAZ-E’FO TAAA-EFATAM MINHUM YOZABBEHO ABNAAA-AHUM WA YASTAHYEE NESAAA-AHUM, INNAHU KAANA MENAL MUFSEDEEN.\nIndeed Pharaoh tyrannized over the land, reducing its people to factions, abasing one group of them, slaughtering their sons, and sparing their women. Indeed, He was one of the agents of corruption.\nوَنُرِيْدُ اَنْ نَّمُنَّ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَنَجْعَلَهُمْ اَئِمَّةً وَّنَجْعَلَهُمُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَۙ‏(5)\nWA NOREEDO AN NAMUNNA A’LAL LAZEENAZ TUZ-E’FOO FIL ARZE WA NAJA’LAHUM AIMMATAWN WA NAJ-A’LAHOMUL WAARESEEN.\nAnd We desired to show favour to those who were abased in the land, and to make them imams, and to make them the heirs,\nوَنُمَكِّنَ لَهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَنُرِىَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ وَجُنُوْدَهُمَا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَحْذَرُوْنَ‏(6)\nWA NOMAKKENA LAHUM FIL ARZE WA NOREYA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA MINHUM MAA KAANOO YAHZAROON.\nand to establish them in the land, and to show Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts from them that of which they were apprehensive.\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمِّ مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَرْضِعِيْهِ‌ۚ فَاِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَاَ لْقِيْهِ فِى الْيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِىْ وَلَا تَحْزَنِىْۚ اِنَّا رَآدُّوْهُ اِلَيْكِ وَجٰعِلُوْهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(7)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA UMME MOOSAA AN ARZE-E’EH, FA-EZAA KHIFTE A’LAYHE FA-ALQEEHE FIL YAMME WA LAA TAKHAAFEE WA LAA TAHZANEE, INNAA RAAADDOOHO ELAYKE WA JAA-E’LOOHO MENAL MURSALEEN.\nWe revealed to Moses’ mother, [saying], ‘Nurse him; then, when you fear for him, cast him into the river, and do not fear or grieve, for We will restore him to you and make him one of the apostles.’\nفَالْتَقَطَهٗۤ اٰلُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُوْنَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَّحَزَنًا ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ وَجُنُوْدَهُمَا كَانُوْا خٰطِئِيْنَ‏(8)\nFALTAQATAHU AALO FIRA’UNA LEYAKOONA LAHUM A’DUWWAWN WA HAZANAA, INNA FIR-A’UNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA KAANOO KHAATE-EEN.\nThen Pharaoh’s kinsmen picked him up that he might be an enemy and a cause of grief to them. Indeed Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts were iniquitous.\nوَقَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ فِرْعَوْنَ قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّىْ وَلَكَ‌ ؕ لَا تَقْتُلُوْهُ ‌ۖ  عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّنْفَعَنَاۤ اَوْ نَتَّخِذَهٗ وَلَدًا وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA QAALATIM RA-ATO FIRA’UNA WA HAAMAANA WA JONOODAHOMAA KAANOO KHAATE-EEN.\nPharaoh’s wife said [to him], ‘[This infant will be] a [source of] comfort to me and to you. Do not kill him. Maybe he will benefit us, or we will adopt him as a son.’ But they were not aware.\nوَاَصْبَحَ فُؤَادُ اُمِّ مُوْسٰى فٰرِغًا‌ ؕ اِنْ كَادَتْ لَتُبْدِىْ بِهٖ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ رَّبَطْنَا عَلٰى قَلْبِهَا لِتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA ASBAHA FOWAADO UMME MOOSAA FAAREGHAA, IN KAADAT LATUBDEE BEHI LAWLAA AR RABATNAA A’LAA QALBEHAA LETAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nThe heart of Moses’ mother became desolate, and indeed she was about to divulge it had We not fortified her heart so that she might have faith [in Allah’s promise].\nوَقَالَتْ لِاُخْتِهٖ قُصِّيْهِ‌ فَبَصُرَتْ بِهٖ عَنْ جُنُبٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nWA QAALAT LEUKHTEHI QUSSEEHE, FABASORAT BEHI A’N JONOBIWN WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nShe said to his sister, ‘Follow him.’ So she watched him from a distance, while they were not aware.\nوَحَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَرَاضِعَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَقَالَتْ هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَهْلِ بَيْتٍ يَّكْفُلُوْنَهٗ لَكُمْ وَهُمْ لَهٗ نٰصِحُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIL MARAAZE-A’ MIN QABLO FAQAALAT HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA AHLE BAYTIYN YAKFOLOONAHU LAKUM WA HUM LAHU NAASEHOON.\nSince before We had forbidden him to be suckled by any nurse. So she said, ‘Shall I show you a household that will take care of him for you and they will be his well-wishers?’\nفَرَدَدْنٰهُ اِلٰٓى اُمِّهٖ كَىْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ وَلِتَعْلَمَ اَنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(13)\nFARADADNAAHO ELAA UMMEHI KAY TAQARRA A’YNOHAA WA LAA TAHZANA WA LETA’TAMA ANNA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThat is how We restored him to his mother so that she might be comforted and not grieve, and that she might know that Allah’s promise is true, but most of them do not know.\nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَاسْتَوٰٓى اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا‌ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(14)\nWA LAMMAA BALAGHA ASHUDDAHU WAS-TAWAA AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA, WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nWhen he came of age and became fully matured, We gave him judgement and knowledge, and thus do We reward the virtuous.\nوَدَخَلَ الْمَدِيْنَةَ عَلٰى حِيْنِ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ اَهْلِهَا فَوَجَدَ فِيْهَا رَجُلَيْنِ يَقْتَتِلٰنِ  هٰذَا مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ وَهٰذَا مِنْ عَدُوِّهٖ‌ۚ فَاسْتَغَاثَهُ الَّذِىْ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ عَلَى الَّذِىْ مِنْ عَدُوِّهٖۙ فَوَكَزَهٗ مُوْسٰى فَقَضٰى عَلَيْهِ‌  قَالَ هٰذَا مِنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطٰنِ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَدُوٌّ مُّضِلٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(15)\nWA DAKHALAL MADEENATA A’LAA HEENE GHAFLATIM MIN AHLEHAA FAWAJADA FEEHAA RAJOLAYNE YAQTATELAANE, HAAZAA MIN SHEE-A’TEHI WA HAAZAA MIN A’DUWWEH, FASTAGHAASAHUL LAZEE MIN SHEE-A’TEHE A’LAL LAZEE MIN A’DUWWEHI, FAWAKAZAHU MOOSAA FAQAZAA A’LAYHE, QAALA HAAZAA MIN A’MALISH SHAYTAAN, INNAHU A’DUWWUM MOZILLUM MOBEEN.\n[One day] he entered the city at a time when its people were not likely to take notice. He found there two men fighting, this one from among his followers, and that one from his enemies. The one who was from his followers sought his help against him who was from his enemies. So Moses hit him with his fist, whereupon he expired. He said, ‘This is of Satan’s doing. Indeed he is clearly a misguiding enemy.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِىْ فَاغْفِرْ لِىْ فَغَفَرَ لَهٗ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(16)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE ZALAMTO NAFSEE FAGH-FIR LEE FA-GHAFARA LAHU, INNAHU HOWAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! I have wronged myself. Forgive me!’ So He forgave him. Indeed, He is the All-forgiving, the All-merciful.\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَاۤ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ فَلَنْ اَكُوْنَ ظَهِيْرًا لِّلْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(17)\nQAALA RABBE BEMAA AN-A’MTA A’LAYYA FALAN AKOONA ZAHEERAL LILMUJREMEEN.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! As You have blessed me, I will never be a supporter of the guilty.’\nفَاَصْبَحَ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ خَآئِفًا يَّتَرَقَّبُ فَاِذَا الَّذِى اسْتَنْصَرَهٗ بِالْاَمْسِ يَسْتَصْرِخُهٗ‌ ؕ قَالَ لَهٗ مُوْسٰٓى اِنَّكَ لَغَوِىٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(18)\nFA-ASBAHA FIL MADEENATE KHAAA-EFAYN YATARAQQABO FA-EZAL LAZIS TANSARAHU BIL-AMSE YASTASREKHOH, QAALA LAHU MOOSAA INNAKA LA-GHAWIYYUM MOBEEN.\nHe rose at dawn in the city, fearful and vigilant, when behold, the one who had sought his help the day before, shouted for his help [once again]. Moses said to him, ‘You are indeed clearly perverse!’\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يَّبْطِشَ بِالَّذِىْ هُوَ عَدُوٌّ لَّهُمَا ۙ قَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اَ تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَقْتُلَنِىْ كَمَا قَتَلْتَ نَفْسًۢا بِالْاَمْسِ ‌ۖ  اِنْ تُرِيْدُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ جَبَّارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِيْنَ‏(19)\nFALAMMAA AN ARAADA AYN YABTESHA BIL-LAZEE HOWA A’DUWWUL LAHOMAA, QAALA MOOSAA ATOREEDO AN TAQTOLANEE KAMAA QATALTA NAFSAM BIL AMS, IN TOREEDO ILLAA AN TAKOONA JABBAARAN FIL ARZE WA MAA TOREEDO AN TAKOONA MENAL MUSLEHEEN.\nBut when he wanted to strike him who was an enemy of both of them, he said, ‘Moses, do you want to kill me, just like the one you killed yesterday? You only want to be a tyrant in the land, and you do not desire to be one who brings about reform.’\nوَجَآءَ رَجُلٌ مِّنْ اَقْصَا الْمَدِيْنَةِ يَسْعٰى قَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنَّ الْمَلَاَ يَاْتَمِرُوْنَ بِكَ لِيَقْتُلُوْكَ فَاخْرُجْ اِنِّىْ لَكَ مِنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA JAAA-A RAJOLUM MIN AQSAL MADEENATE YAS-A’A, QAALA YAA MOOSAA INNAL MALA-A YAATAMEROONA BEKA LEYAQTOLOOKA FAKHRUJ INNEE LAKA MENAN NAASEHEEN.\nThere came a man from the city outskirts, hurrying. He said, ‘Moses! The elite are indeed conspiring to kill you. So leave. I am indeed your well-wisher.’\nفَخَرَجَ مِنْهَا خَآئِفًا يَّتَرَقَّبُ‌ قَالَ رَبِّ نَجِّنِىْ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(21)\nFAKHARAJA MINHAA KHAAA-EFAYN YATARAQQABO, QAALA RABBE NAJJENEE MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nSo he left the city, fearful and vigilant. He said, ‘My Lord! Deliver me from the wrongdoing lot.’\nوَلَمَّا تَوَجَّهَ تِلْقَآءَ مَدْيَنَ قَالَ عَسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَنْ يَّهْدِيَنِىْ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(22)\nWA LAMMAA TAWAJJAHA TILQAAA-A MADYANA QAALA A’SAA RABBEE AYN YAHDEYANEE SAWAAA-AS SABEEL.\nAnd when he turned his face toward Midian, he said, ‘Maybe my Lord will show me the right way.’\nوَلَمَّا وَرَدَ مَآءَ مَدْيَنَ وَجَدَ عَلَيْهِ اُمَّةً مِّنَ النَّاسِ يَسْقُوْنَ  وَوَجَدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمُ امْرَاَتَيْنِ تَذُوْدٰنِ‌ ۚ قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُمَا‌ ؕ قَالَتَا لَا نَسْقِىْ حَتّٰى يُصْدِرَ الرِّعَآءُ‌ وَاَبُوْنَا شَيْخٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(23)\nWA LAMMAA WARADA MAAA-A MADYANA WAJADA A’LAYHE UMMATAM MENAN NAASE YASQOON, WA WAJADA MIN DOONEHEMUM RA-ATAYNE TAZOODAAN, QAALA MAA KHATBOKOMAA, QAALATAA LAA NASQEE HATTAA YUSDERAR RE-A’AA, WA ABOONAA SHAYKUN KABEER.\nWhen he arrived at the well of Midian, he found there a throng of people watering [their flocks], and he found, besides them, two women holding back [their flock]. He said, ‘What is your business?’ They said, ‘We do not water [our flock] until the shepherds have driven out [their flocks], and our father is an aged man.’\nفَسَقٰى لَهُمَا ثُمَّ تَوَلّٰٓى اِلَى الظِّلِّ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ لِمَاۤ اَنْزَلْتَ اِلَىَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيْرٌ‏(24)\nFASAQAA LAHOMAA SUMMA TAWALLAA ELAZ ZILLE FAQAALA RABBE INNEE LEMAA ANZALTA ELAYYA MIN KHAYRIN FAQEER.\nSo he watered [their flock] for them. Then he withdrew toward the shade and said, ‘My Lord! I am indeed in need of any good You may send down to me!’\nفَجَآءَتْهُ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا تَمْشِىْ عَلَى اسْتِحْيَآءٍ  قَالَتْ اِنَّ اَبِىْ يَدْعُوْكَ لِيَجْزِيَكَ اَجْرَ مَا سَقَيْتَ لَنَا‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهٗ وَقَصَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَصَصَ ۙ قَالَ لَا تَخَفْ‌ نَجَوْتَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(25)\nFA-JAAA-ATHO EHDAAHOMAA TAMSHEE A’LAS TEHYAAA, QAALAT INNA ABEE YADO’OKA LEYAJZEYAKA AJRA MAA SAQAYTA LANAA, FALAMMAA JAAA-AHU WA QASSA A’LAYHIL QASASA, QAALA LAA TAKHAF, NAJAWTA MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen one of the two women approached him, walking bashfully. She said, ‘Indeed my father invites you to pay you the wages for watering [our flock] for us.’ So when he came to him and recounted the story to him, he said, ‘Do not be afraid. You have been delivered from the wrongdoing lot.’\nقَالَتْ اِحْدٰٮہُمَا يٰۤاَبَتِ اسْتَاْجِرْهُ‌ اِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَاْجَرْتَ الْقَوِىُّ الْاَمِيْنُ‏(26)\nQAALAT EHDAAHOMAA YAA ABATIS TAAJIRHO, INNA KHAYRA MANIS TAAJARTAL QAWIYYUL AMEEN.\nOne of the two women said, ‘Father, hire him. Indeed the best you can hire is a powerful and trustworthy man.’\nقَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُنْكِحَكَ اِحْدَى ابْنَتَىَّ هٰتَيْنِ عَلٰٓى اَنْ تَاْجُرَنِىْ ثَمٰنِىَ حِجَجٍ‌ۚ فَاِنْ اَتْمَمْتَ عَشْرًا فَمِنْ عِنْدِكَ‌ۚ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اَشُقَّ عَلَيْكَ‌ؕ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(27)\nQAALA INNEE OREEDO AN UNKEHAKA EHDAB NATAYYA HAATAYNE A’LAA AN TAAJORANEE SAMAANEYA HEJAJ, FA-IN ATMAMTA A’SHRAN FAMIN I’NDEK, WA MAA OREEDO AN ASHUQQA A’LAYK, SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nHe said, ‘Indeed I desire to marry you to one of these two daughters of mine, on condition that you hire yourself to me for eight years. And if you complete ten, that will be up to you, and I do not want to be hard on you. God willing, you will find me to a righteous person.’\nقَالَ ذٰ لِكَ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكَ‌ ؕ اَيَّمَا الْاَجَلَيْنِ قَضَيْتُ فَلَا عُدْوَانَ عَلَىَّ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِيْلٌ‏(28)\nQAALA ZAALEKA BAYNEE WA BAYNAK, AYYAMAL AJALAYNE QAZAYTO FALAA U’DWAANA A’LAY, WAL LAAHO A’LAA MAA NAQOOLO WAKEEL.\nHe said, ‘This will be [by consent] between you and me. Whichever of the two terms I complete, there shall be no imposition upon me, and Allah is witness over what we say.’\nفَلَمَّا قَضٰى مُوْسَى الْاَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِاَهْلِهٖۤ اٰنَسَ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ نَارًا‌ۚ قَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا‌ لَّعَلِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ اَوْ جَذْوَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nFALAMMAA QAZAA MOOSAL AJALA WA SAARA BE-AHLEHI AANASA MIN JAANEBIT TOORE NAARAA, QAALA LE-AHLEHIM KOSOO INNEE AANASTO NAARAL LA-A’LLEE AATEEKUM MINHAA BEKHABARIN AW JAZWATIM MENAN NAARE LA-A’LLAKUM TASTALOON.\nSo when Moses completed the term and set out with his family, he descried a fire on the side of the mountain. He said to his family, ‘Wait! Indeed, I descry a fire! Maybe I will bring you some news from it, or a brand of fire so that you may warm yourselves.’\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَتٰٮهَا نُوْدِىَ مِنْ شَاطِئِ الْوَادِ الْاَيْمَنِ فِى الْبُقْعَةِ الْمُبٰرَكَةِ مِنَ الشَّجَرَةِ اَنْ يّٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ۙ‏(30)\nFALAMMAA ATAAHAA NOODEYA MIN SHAATEIL WAATIL AYMANE FIL BUQ-A’TIL MOBAARAKATE MENASH SHAJARATE AYN YAA MOOSAA INNEE ANAL LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhen he approached it, he was called from the right bank of the valley in that blessed site from the tree: ‘Moses! Indeed I am Allah, the Lord of all the worlds!’\nوَاَنْ اَ لْقِ عَصَاكَ‌ ؕ فَلَمَّا رَاٰهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَاَنَّهَا جَآنٌّ وَّلّٰى مُدْبِرًا وَّلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ‌ ؕ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اَ قْبِلْ وَلَا تَخَفْ‌ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الْاٰمِنِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA AN ALQE A’SAAK, FALAMMAA RA-AAHAA TAHTAZZO KA-ANNAHAA JAAANNUWN WALLAA MUDBERAWN WA LAM YO-A’QQIB, YAA MOOSAA AQBIL WA LAA TAKHAF, INNAKA MENAL AAMENEEN.\nAnd: ‘Throw down your staff!’ And when he saw it wriggling as if it were a snake, he turned his back [to flee], without looking back. ‘Moses! Come forward, and do not be afraid. Indeed you are safe.’\nاُسْلُكْ يَدَكَ فِىْ جَيْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ وَّاضْمُمْ اِلَيْكَ جَنَاحَكَ مِنَ الرَّهْبِ‌ فَذٰنِكَ بُرْهَانٰنِ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏‏‏(32)\nUSLUK YADAKA FEE JAYBEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAYRE SOOO-IWN WAZMUM ELAYKA JANAAHAKA MENAR RAHBE FAZAANEKA BURHAANAANE MIR RABBEKA ELAA FIR-A’WNA WA MALAA-EH, INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\n‘Insert your hand into your shirt. It will emerge white, without any fault, and keep your arms drawn in awe to your sides. These shall be two proofs from your Lord to Pharaoh and his elite. They are indeed a transgressing lot.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ قَتَلْتُ مِنْهُمْ نَفْسًا فَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّقْتُلُوْنِ‏(33)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE QATALTO MINHUM NAFSAN FA AKHAAFO AYN YAQTOLOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Indeed, I have killed one of their men, so I fear they will kill me.\nوَاَخِىْ هٰرُوْنُ هُوَ اَفْصَحُ مِنِّىْ لِسَانًا فَاَرْسِلْهُ مَعِىَ رِدْاً يُّصَدِّقُنِىْٓ‌ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْنِ‏(34)\nWA AKHEE HAAROONO HOWA AFSAHO MINNEE LESAANAN FA-ARSILHO MA-E’YA RID-AYN YOSADDEQONEE, INNEE AKHAAFO AYN YOKAZZEBOON.\nAaron, my brother—he is more eloquent than me in speech. So send him with me as a helper to confirm me, for I fear that they will impugn me.’\nقَالَ سَنَشُدُّ عَضُدَكَ بِاَخِيْكَ وَنَجْعَلُ لَكُمَا سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا يَصِلُوْنَ اِلَيْكُمَا‌‌ ۛ ‌ۚ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ ‌ ۛ‌ ۚ اَنْتُمَا وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَكُمَا الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(35)\nQAALA SANASHUDDO A’ZODAKA BEAKHEEKA WA NAJ-A’LO LAKOMAA SULTAANAN FALAA YASELOONA ELAYKOMAA, BEAAYAATENAA, ANTOMAA WA MANIT TABA-A’KOMAL GHAALEBOON.\nHe said, ‘We will strengthen your arm by means of your brother, and invest both of you with such authority that they will not touch you. With the help of Our signs, you two, and those who follow the two of you, shall be the victors.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّفْتَرًى وَمَا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِىْۤ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(36)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA BAYYENAATIN QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MUFTARAWN WA MAA SAMEA’NAA BEHAAZAA FEE AABAAA-ENAL AWWALEEN.\nWhen Moses brought them Our manifest signs, they said, ‘This is nothing but concocted magic. We never heard of such a thing among our forefathers.’\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى رَبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْهُدٰى مِنْ عِنْدِهٖ وَمَنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA RABBEE A-A’LAMO BEMAN JAAA-A BILHODAA MIN I’NDEHI WA MAN TAKOONO LAHU A’AQEBATUD DAAR, INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nMoses said, ‘My Lord knows best who brings guidance from Him, and in whose favour the outcome of that abode will be. The wrongdoers will not be felicitous.’\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَاُ مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرِىْ‌ ۚ فَاَوْقِدْ لِىْ يٰهَامٰنُ عَلَى الطِّيْنِ فَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَطَّلِعُ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰى ۙ وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(38)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O MAA A’LIMTO LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYREE, FA-AW-QID LEE YAAHAAMAANO A’LAT TEENE FAJ-A’L LEE SARHAL LA-A’LLEE AT-TALE-O’ ELAA ELAAHE MOOSAA, WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOHU MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nPharaoh said, ‘O [members of the] elite! I do not know of any god that you may have besides me. Haman, light for me a fire over clay, and build me a tower so that I may take a look at Moses’ god, and indeed I consider him to be a liar!’\nوَاسْتَكْبَرَ هُوَ وَجُنُوْدُهٗ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اِلَيْنَا لَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(39)\nWASTAKBARA HOWA WA JONOODOHU FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA ZANNOO ANNAHUM ELAYNAA LAA YARJEO’ON.\nHe and his hosts unduly acted arrogantly in the land, and thought they would not be brought back to Us.\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ‌ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(40)\nFA-AKHAZNAAHO WA JONOODOHU FANABAZNAAHUM FIL YAM, FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUZ ZAALEMEEN.\nSo We seized him and his hosts, and threw them into the sea. So observe how was the fate of the wrongdoers!\nوَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّدْعُوْنَ اِلَى النَّارِ‌ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(41)\nWA JA-A’LNAAHUM AIMMATAYN YAD-O’ONA ELAN NAAR, WA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE LAA YUNSAROON.\nWe made them leaders who invite to the Fire, and on the Day of Resurrection they will not receive any help.\nوَاَتْبَعْنٰهُمْ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً‌  ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ هُمْ مِّنَ الْمَقْبُوْحِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA ATBA’NAAHUM FEE HAAZEHID DUNYAA LA’NAH, WA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE HUM MENAL MAQBOOHEEN.\nWe made a curse pursue them in this world, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be among the disfigured.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا الْقُرُوْنَ الْاُوْلٰى بَصَآئِرَ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA MIM BA’DE MAA AHLAKNAL QOROONAL OOLAA BASAAA-ERA LINNAASE WA HODAWN WA RAHMATAL LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book, after We had destroyed the former generations, as [a set of] eye-openers, guidance and mercy for mankind, so that they may take admonition.\nوَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الْغَرْبِىِّ اِذْ قَضَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسَى الْاَمْرَ وَمَا كُنْتَ مِنَ الشّٰهِدِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWA MAA KUNTA BEJAANEBIL GHARBIYYE IZ QAZAYNAA ELAA MOOSAL AMRA WA MAA KUNTA MENASH SHAAHEDEEN.\nYou were not on the western side when We revealed the commandments to Moses, nor were you among the witnesses.\nوَلٰكِنَّاۤ اَنْشَاْنَا قُرُوْنًا فَتَطَاوَلَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْعُمُرُ‌ۚ وَمَا كُنْتَ ثَاوِيًا فِىْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ تَتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَاۙ وَلٰكِنَّا كُنَّا مُرْسِلِيْنَ‏(45)\nWA LAAKINNAA ANSHAANAA QOROONAN FATATAAWALA A’LAYHEMUL O’MOR, WA MAA KUNTA SAAWEYAN FEE AHLE MADYANA TATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA, WA LAAKINNAA KUNNAA MURSALEEN.\nBut We brought forth other generations and time took its toll on them. You did not dwell among the people of Midian reciting to them Our signs, but it is We who are the senders [of the apostles].\nوَمَا كُنْتَ بِجَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ اِذْ نَادَيْنَا وَلٰكِنْ رَّحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اَتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA MAA KUNTA BEJAANEBIT TOORE IZ NAADAYNAA WA LAAKIR RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA LETUNZERA QAWMAM MAA ATAAHUM MIN NAZEERIM MIN QABLEKA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd you were not on the side of the Mount when We called out [to Moses], but [We have sent you as] a mercy from your Lord that you may warn a people to whom there did not come any warner before you, so that they may take admonition.\nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ تُصِيْبَهُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُوْا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَاۤ اَرْسَلْتَ اِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا فَنَتَّبِعَ اٰيٰتِكَ وَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA LAWLAA AN TOSEEBAHUM MOSEEBATUM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM FAYAQOOLOO RABBANAA LAWLAA ARSALTA ELAYNAA RASOOLAN FANATTABE-A’ AAYAATEKA WA NAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd lest—if an affliction were to befall them because of what their hands have sent ahead —they should say, ‘Our Lord! Why did You not send us an apostle so that we might have followed Your signs and been among the faithful?’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى‌ ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ ‌ۚ قَالُوْا سِحْرٰنِ تَظَاهَرَا وَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِكُلٍّ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(48)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO LAWLAA OOTEYA MISLA MAA OOTEYA MOOSAA, AWALAM YAKFOROO BEMAA OOTEYA MOOSAA MIN QABL, QAALOO SEHRAANE TAZAAHARAA, WA QAALOO INNAA BEKULLIN KAAFEROON.\nBut when there came to them the truth from Us, they said, ‘Why has he not been given the like of what Moses was given?’ Did they not disbelieve what Moses was given before, and said, ‘Two magicians abetting each other,’ and said, ‘Indeed we disbelieve both of them’?\nقُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبٍ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ هُوَ اَهْدٰى مِنْهُمَاۤ اَتَّبِعْهُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(49)\nQUL FAATOO BEKETAABIM MIN I’NDIL LAAHE HOWA AHDAA MINHOMAA ATTABE’HO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay, ‘If you are truthful, bring some Book from Allah better in guidance than the two on them so that I may follow it.’\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكَ فَاعْلَمْ اَنَّمَا يَتَّبِعُوْنَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ اَضَلُّ مِمَّنِ اتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ بِغَيْرِ هُدًى مِّنَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(50)\nFA-IL LAM YASTAJEEBOO LAKA FA’LAM ANNAMAA YATTABE-O’ONA AHWAAA-AHUM, WA MAN AZALLO MIMMANIT TABA-A’ HAWAAHO BEGHAYRE HODAM MENAL LAAH, INNAL LAAH LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen if they do not respond to you[r] [summons], know that they only follow their desires, and who is more astray than him who follows his desires without any guidance from Allah? Indeed Allah does not guide the wrongdoing lot.\nوَلَقَدْ وَصَّلْنَا لَهُمُ الْقَوْلَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَؕ‏(51)\nWA LAQAD WASSALNAA LAHOMUL QAWLA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nCertainly We have carried on this discourse for them so that they may take admonition.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ هُمْ بِهٖ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\nALLAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA MIN QABLEHI HUM BEHI YOAMENOON.\nThose to whom We gave the Book before it are the ones who believe in it,\nوَاِذَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِهٖۤ اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA EZAA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM QAALOO AAMANNAA BEHI INNAHUL HAQQO MIR RABBENAA INNAA KUNNAA MIN QABLEHI MUSLEMEEN.\nand when it is recited to them, they say, ‘We believe in it. It is indeed the truth from our Lord. Indeed we were Muslims [even] before it [came].’\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْتَوْنَ اَجْرَهُمْ مَّرَّتَيْنِ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا وَيَدْرَءُوْنَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّيِّئَةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(54)\nOOLAAA-EKA YOATAWNA AJRAHUM MARRATAYNE BEMAA SABAROO WA YADRAOONA BILHASANATIS SAYYEATE WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOON.\nThose will be given their reward two times for their patience. They repel evil [conduct] with good, and spend out of what We have provided them,\nوَاِذَا سَمِعُوا اللَّغْوَ اَعْرَضُوْا عَنْهُ وَقَالُوْا لَنَاۤ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ لَا نَبْتَغِى الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(55)\nWA EZAA SAME-O’L LAGHWA A-A’RAZOO A’NHO WA QAALOO LANAA A-A’MAALONAA WA LAKUM A-A’MAALOKUM, SALAAMUN A’LAYKUM, LAA NABTAGHIL JAAHELEEN.\nand when they hear vain talk, they avoid it and say, ‘Our deeds belong to us, and your deeds belong to you. Peace be to you. We do not court the ignorant.’\nاِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِىْ مَنْ اَحْبَبْتَ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ؕ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(56)\nINNAKA LAA TAHDEE MAN AHBABTA WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAHDEE MAYN YASHAAA, WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nYou cannot guide whomever you wish, but [it is] Allah [who] guides whomever He wishes, and He knows best those who are guided.\nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ نَّتَّبِعِ الْهُدٰى مَعَكَ نُتَخَطَّفْ مِنْ اَرْضِنَا ؕ اَوَلَمْ نُمَكِّنْ لَّهُمْ حَرَمًا اٰمِنًا يُّجْبٰٓى اِلَيْهِ ثَمَرٰتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ رِّزْقًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA QAALOO IN NATTABE-I’L HODAA MA-A’KA NOTAKHATTAF MIN ARZENAA, AWALAM NOMAKKIL LAHUM HARAMAN AAMENAYN YUJBAA ELAYHE SAMARAATO KULLE SHAY-IR RIZQAM MIL LADUNNAA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThey say, ‘If we follow the guidance with you, we will be forced out of our territory.’ Did We not establish a secure sanctuary for them where fruits of all kinds are brought as a provision from Us? But most of them do not know.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍۢ بَطِرَتْ مَعِيْشَتَهَا ‌ۚ فَتِلْكَ مَسٰكِنُهُمْ لَمْ تُسْكَنْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا ؕ وَكُنَّا نَحْنُ الْوٰرِثِيْنَ‏(58)\nWA KAM AHLAKNAA MIN QARYATIM BATERAT MA-E’ESHATAHAA, FATILKA MASAAKENOHUM LAM TUSKAM MIM BA’DEHIM ILLAA QALEELA, WA KUNNAA NAHNUL WAARESEEN.\nHow many a town We have destroyed that exulted in its lifestyle! There lie their dwellings, uninhabited after them except by a few, and We were the [sole] inheritors.\nوَ مَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ مُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى حَتّٰى يَبْعَثَ فِىْۤ اُمِّهَا رَسُوْلًا يَّتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَا‌ ۚ وَمَا كُنَّا مُهْلِكِى الْقُرٰٓى اِلَّا وَاَهْلُهَا ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(59)\nWA MAA KAANA RABBOKA MOHLEKAL KORAA HATTAA YAB-A’SA FEE UMMEHAA RASOOLAYN YATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA, WA MAA KUNNAA MOHLEKIL QORAA ILLAA WA AHLOHAA ZAALEMOON.\nYour Lord would not destroy the towns until He had raised an apostle in their mother city to recite to them Our signs. We would never destroy the towns except when their people were wrongdoers.\nوَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَمَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَزِيْنَتُهَا‌ ۚ وَمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA MAA OOTEETUM MIN SHAY-IN FAMATAAUL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA ZEENATOHAA, WA MAA I’NDAL LAAHE KHAYRUWN WA ABQAA, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nWhatever things you have been given are only the wares of the life of this world and its glitter, and what is with Allah is better and more lasting. Will you not exercise your reason?\nاَفَمَنْ وَّعَدْنٰهُ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا فَهُوَ لَاقِيْهِ كَمَنْ مَّتَّعْنٰهُ مَتَاعَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ هُوَ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(61)\nAFAMAWN WA-A’DNAAHO WA’DAN HASANAN FAHOWA LAAQEEHE KAMAM MATTA’NAAHO MATAA-A’L HAYAATID DUNYA SUMMA HOWA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE MENAL MOHZAREEN.\nIs he to whom We have given a good promise, which he will receive, like him whom We have provided the wares of the life of this world, but who will be arraigned on the Day of Resurrection?\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nThe day He will call out to them and ask, ‘Where are My ‘partners’ that you used to claim?’\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَوْلُ رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَغْوَيْنَا ۚ اَغْوَيْنٰهُمْ كَمَا غَوَيْنَا‌ ۚ تَبَرَّاْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ‌ مَا كَانُوْۤا اِيَّانَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(63)\nQAALAL LAZEENA HAQQA A’LAYHEMUL QAWLO RABBANAA HAA-OLAAA-IL LAZEENA AGHWAYNAA, AGHWAYNAAHUM KAMAA GHAWAYNAA, TABARRAANAA ELAYK, MAA KAANOO IYYAANAA YA’BODOON.\nThose against whom the word had become due will say, ‘Our Lord! These are the ones whom we have perverted. We perverted them as we were perverse ourselves. We repudiate them before You: it was not us that they worshipped.’\nوَقِيْلَ ادْعُوْا شُرَكَآءَكُمْ فَدَعَوْهُمْ فَلَمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَهُمْ وَرَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ‌ۚ لَوْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA QEELAD O’O SHORAKAAA-AKUM FADA-A’WHUM FALAM YASTAJEEBOO LAHUM WA RA-AWUL A’ZAAB, LAW ANNAHUM KAANOO YAHTADOON.\nIt will be said, ‘Invoke your partners!’ So they will invoke them, but they will not respond to them, and they will sight the punishment, wishing they had followed guidance.\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ مَاذَاۤ اَجَبْتُمُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(65)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO MAA ZAA AJABTOMUL MURSALEEN.\nThe day He will call out to them and say, ‘What response did you give to the apostles?’\nفَعَمِيَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَنْۢبَآءُ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَهُمْ لَا يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(66)\nFA-A’MEYAT A’LAYHEMUL AMBAAA-O YAWMA-EZIN FAHUM LAA YATASAAA-ALOON.\nThat day all information will be withheld from them, so they will not question one another.\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَعَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُفْلِحِيْنَ‏(67)\nFA-AMMAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-A’SAA AYN YAKOONA MENAL MUFLEHEEN.\nAs for him who repents, has faith and acts righteously, maybe he will be among the felicitous.\nوَرَبُّكَ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيَخْتَارُ‌ؕ مَا كَانَ لَهُمُ الْخِيَرَةُ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA RABBOKA YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA-O WA YAKHTAAR, MAA KAANA LAHOMUL KHEYARAH, SUBHAANAL LAAHE WA TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nYour Lord creates whatever He wishes and chooses: they have no choice. Immaculate is Allah and exalted above [having] any partners that they ascribe [to Him].\nوَرَبُّكَ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُوْرُهُمْ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA RABBOKA YA’LAMO MAA TOKINNO SODOOROHUM WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nYour Lord knows whatever their breasts conceal, and whatever they disclose.\nوَهُوَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ؕ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِى الْاُوْلٰى وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَلَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(70)\nWA HOWAL LAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, LAHUL HAMDO FIL OOLAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA LAHUL HUKMO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nHe is Allah, there is no god except Him. All praise belongs to Him in this world and the Hereafter. All judgement belongs to Him, and to Him you will be brought back.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمُ الَّيْلَ سَرْمَدًا اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِضِيَآءٍ‌ؕاَفَلَا تَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(71)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN JA-A’LAL LAAHO A’LAYKOMUL LAYLA SARMADAN ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRUL LAAHE YAATEEKUM BEZEYAAA, AFALAA TASMA-O’ON.\nSay, ‘Tell me, if Allah were to make the night perpetual for you until the Day of Resurrection, what god other than Allah can bring you light? Will you not listen?’\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمُ النَّهَارَ سَرْمَدًا اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِلَيْلٍ تَسْكُنُوْنَ فِيْهِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(72)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN JA-A’LAL LAAHO A’LAYKOMUN NAHAARA SARMADAN ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRUL LAAHE YAATEEKUM BELAYLIN TASKONOONA FEEH, AFALAA TUBSEROON.\nSay, ‘Tell me, if Allah were to make the day perpetual for you until the Day of Resurrection, what god other than Allah can bring you night wherein you can rest? Will you not perceive?’\nوَمِنْ رَّحْمَتِهٖ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(73)\nWA MIR RAHMATEHI JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA LETASKONOO FEEHE WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nHe has made for you the night and the day out of His mercy, so that you may rest therein and that you may seek His bounty and so that you may give thanks.\nوَيَوْمَ يُنَادِيْهِمْ فَيَقُوْلُ اَيْنَ شُرَكَآءِىَ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA YAWMA YONAADEEHIM FAYAQOOLO AYNA SHORAKAAA-EYAL LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nThe day He will call out to them and say, ‘Where are My ‘partners’ that you used to claim?’\nوَنَزَعْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ شَهِيْدًا فَقُلْنَا هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ فَعَلِمُوْۤا اَنَّ الْحَقَّ لِلّٰهِ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA NAZA’NAA MIN KULLE UMMATIN SHAHEEDAN FAQULNAA HAATOO BURHAANAKUM FA-A’LEMOO ANNAL HAQQA LILLAAHE WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nWe shall draw from every nation a witness and say, ‘Produce your evidence.’ Then they will know that all reality belongs to Allah and what they used to fabricate will forsake them.\nاِنَّ قَارُوْنَ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمِ مُوْسٰى فَبَغٰى عَلَيْهِمْ‌ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْكُنُوْزِ مَاۤ اِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهٗ لَتَنُوْٓاُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ اُولِى الْقُوَّةِ اِذْ قَالَ لَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ لَا تَفْرَحْ‌ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْفَرِحِيْنَ‏(76)\nINNA QAAROONA KAANA MIN QAWME MOOSAA FABAGHAA A’LAYHIM, WA AATAYNAAHO MENAL KONOOZE MAA INNA MAFAATEHAHU LATANOOO-O BIL-U’SBATE OOLIL QUWWAH, IZ QAALA LAHU QAWMOHU LAA TAFRAH INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL FAREHEEN.\nKorah indeed belonged to the people of Moses, but he bullied them. We had given him so much treasures that their chests indeed proved heavy for a band of stalwarts. When his people said to him, ‘Do not boast! Indeed Allah does not like the boasters.\nوَابْتَغِ فِيْمَاۤ اٰتٰٮكَ اللّٰهُ الدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ‌ وَلَا تَنْسَ نَصِيْبَكَ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا‌ وَاَحْسِنْ كَمَاۤ اَحْسَنَ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْكَ‌ وَلَا تَبْغِ الْفَسَادَ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(77)\nWABTAGHE FEEMAA AATAAKAL LAAHUD DAARAL AAKHERATA WA LAA TANSA NASEEBAKA MENAD DUNYAA WA AHSIN KAMAA AHSANAL LAAHO ELAYKA WA LAA TABGHIL FASAADA FIL ARZ, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MUFSEDEEN.\nSeek the abode of the Hereafter by means of what Allah has given you, while not forgetting your share of this world. Be good [to others] just as Allah has been good to you, and do not try to cause corruption in the land. Indeed Allah does not like the agents of corruption.’\nقَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُهٗ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ عِنْدِىْ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ اَهْلَكَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مَنْ هُوَ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةً وَّاَكْثَرُ جَمْعًا‌ؕ وَلَا يُسْئَلُ عَنْ ذُنُوْبِهِمُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(78)\nQAALA INNAMAA OOTEETOHU A’LAA I’LMIN I’NDEE, AWALAM YA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA QAD AHLAKA MIN QABLEHI MENAL QOROONE MAN HOWA ASHADDO MINHO QUWWATAW WA AKSARO JAM-A’, WA LAA YUSALO A’N ZONOOBEHEMUL MUJREMOON.\nHe said, ‘I have indeed been given [all] this because of the knowledge that I have.’ Did he not know that Allah had already destroyed before him some of the generations who were more powerful than him and greater in amassing [wealth]? The guilty will not be questioned about their sins.\nفَخَرَجَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فِىْ زِيْنَتِهٖ‌ؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا يٰلَيْتَ لَنَا مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ قَارُوْنُۙ اِنَّهٗ لَذُوْ حَظٍّ عَظِيْمٍ‏(79)\nFAKHARAJA A’LAA QAWMEHI FEE ZEENATEH, QAALAL LAZEENA YOREEDOONAL HAYAATAD DUNYAA YAALAYTA LANAA MISLA MAA OOTEYA QAAROONO, INNAHU LAZOO HAZZIN A’ZEEM.\nSo he emerged before his people in his finery. Those who desired the life of the world said, ‘We wish we had like what Korah has been given! Indeed he is greatly fortunate.’\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ وَيْلَكُمْ ثَوَابُ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ۚ وَلَا يُلَقّٰٮهَاۤ اِلَّا الصّٰبِرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LMA WAYLAKUM SAWAABUL LAAHE KHAYRUL LEMAN AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAA, WA LAA YOLAQQAAHAA ILLAS SAABEROON.\nThose who were given knowledge said [to them], ‘Woe to you! Allah’s reward is better for someone who has faith and acts righteously, and no one will receive it except the patient.’\nفَخَسَفْنَا بِهٖ وَبِدَارِهِ الْاَرْضَ فَمَا كَانَ لَهٗ مِنْ فِئَةٍ يَّنْصُرُوْنَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُنْتَصِرِيْنَ‏(81)\nFAKHASAFNAA BEHI WA BEDAAREHIL ARZ, FAMAA KAANA LAHU MIN FE-ATIYN YANSOROONAHU MIN DOONIL LAAH, WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUNTASEREEN.\nSo We caused the earth to swallow him and his house, and he had no party that might protect him from Allah, nor could he rescue himself.\nوَاَصْبَحَ الَّذِيْنَ تَمَنَّوْا مَكَانَهٗ بِالْاَمْسِ يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَيْكَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ۚ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ مَّنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا لَخَسَفَ بِنَا‌ ؕ وَيْكَاَنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA ASBAHAL LAZEENA TAMANNAW MAKAANAHU BIL-AMSE YAQOOLOONA WAYKA-ANNAL LAAHA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAYN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA YAQDER, LAWLAA AM MANNAL LAAHO A’LAYNAA LAKHASAFA BENAA, WAYKA-ANNAHU LAA YUFLEHUL KAAFEROON.\nBy dawn those who longed to be in his place the day before were saying, ‘Don’t you see that Allah expands the provision for whomever He wishes of His servants, and tightens it? Had Allah not shown us favour, He might have made the earth swallow us too. Don’t you see that the faithless do not prosper?’\nتِلْكَ الدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ نَجْعَلُهَا لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُرِيْدُوْنَ عُلُوًّا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فَسَادًا‌ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(83)\nTILKAD DAARUL AAKHERATO NAJ-A’LOHAA LILLAZEENA LAA YOREEDOONA O’LUWWAN FIL ARZE WA LAA FASAADAA, WAL A-A’QEBATO LILMUTTAQEEN.\nThis is the abode of the Hereafter, which We shall grant to those who do not desire to domineer in the earth nor to cause corruption, and the outcome will be in favour of the Godwary.\nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا‌ ۚ وَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزَى الَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(84)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL HASANATE FALAHU KHAYRUM MINHAA, WA MAN JAAA-A BISSAYYEATE FALAA YUJZAL LAZEENA A’MELUS SAYYE-AATE ILLAA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhoever brings virtue shall receive [a reward] better than it, but whoever brings vice—those who commit misdeeds shall not be requited except for what they used to do.\nاِنَّ الَّذِىْ فَرَضَ عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ لَرَآدُّكَ اِلٰى مَعَادٍ‌ ؕ قُلْ رَّبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ مَنْ جَآءَ بِالْهُدٰى وَمَنْ هُوَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(85)\nINNAL LAZEE FARAZA A’LAYKAL QURAANA LARAAAD-DOKA ELAA MA-A’AD, QUR RABBEE A-A’LAMO MAN JAAA-A BILHODAA WA MAN HOWA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nIndeed He who has revealed to you the Quran will surely restore you to the place of return. Say, ‘My Lord knows best him who brings guidance and him who is in manifest error.’\nوَمَا كُنْتَ تَرْجُوْۤا اَنْ يُّلْقٰٓى اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبُ اِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ ظَهِيْرًا لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA MAA KUNTA TARJOO AYN YULQAA ELAYKAL KETAABO ILLAA RAHMATAM MIR RABBEKA FALAA TAKOONANNA ZAHEERAL LIL KAAFEREEN.\nYou did not expect that the Book would be delivered to you; but it was a mercy from your Lord. So do not be ever an advocate of the faithless.\nوَلَا يَصُدُّنَّكَ عَنْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بَعْدَ اِذْ اُنْزِلَتْ اِلَيْكَ‌ وَادْعُ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ‌ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(87)\nWA LAA YASUDDUNNAKA A’N AAYAATIL LAAHE BA’DA IZ UNZELAT ELAYKA WAD-O’ ELAA RABBEKA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nDo not ever let them bar you from Allah’s signs after they have been sent down to you. Invite to your Lord, and never be one of the polytheists.\nوَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ۘ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ كُلُّ شَىْءٍ هَالِكٌ اِلَّا وَجْهَهٗ‌ؕ لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA LAA TAD-O’ MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHAR, LAA ELAAH ILLAA HOO, KULLO SHAY-IN HAALEKUN ILLAA WAJHAH, LAHUL HUKMO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nAnd do not invoke another god besides Allah; there is no god except Him. Everything is to perish except His Face. All judgement belongs to Him, and to Him you will be brought back.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Qasas (The Narrative)\nThere are 88 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah though some scholars say that it was revealed in Madinah. The 58th verse of this Surah was revealed at the time of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)’s migration from Makkah to Madinah.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will get the reward equivalent to the number of people present at the time of Prophet Musa (a.s.) and all the angels will bear witness on his behalf. If one drinks the water in which this Surah has been dissolved, all his problems and worries will be solved.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is a remedy from illness and worries (this can also be done by writing the Surah inside a container and then gathering rain water in the same container)."
}
